; Print the noun of a name phrase with its article
;
; DE is the noun code of a name phrase (bits 12-15 style, bits 0-11 dictionary
; offset). When PhraseMode ($B703) is not 0 the article (or the capital flag
; of a proper name) comes first (#R$743F); then the noun itself is printed
; with its style bits cleared, as a word of print mode 0 (#R$74C1).
;
; DE Noun code of the name phrase
; O:D Style bits cleared
@label=PrintNounWord
c$7478 PUSH DE       ;
 $7479 LD A,($B703)  ; PhraseMode: with article?
 $747C AND A         ;
 $747D CALL NZ,$743F ; PrintArticle
 $7480 POP DE        ;
 $7481 LD A,D        ;
 $7482 AND $0F       ; keep the offset only
 $7484 LD D,A        ;
 $7485 JP $74C1      ; PrintWord
